<title>EGYPT: Egypt amends volume of offer for 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Egypt amends volume of offer for 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egyptian treasury changed the volume of its next offer for 91-day bills to 1.2 billion pounds from 1.7 billion.</p>
<p>The central bank amended the offer, which was originally published on Monday, for auction on May 28 and issue on May 29 when 91-day bills worth 986.125 million pounds mature.</p>
<p>The average yield at the last auction was 8.808 percent.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
</text>
